<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vassal</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as vassalage</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A vassal is a ruler or lord who holds power or land in subordination to a superior, owing loyalty, tribute or military service in return for protection or recognition. Vassalage was a widespread means of extending imperial authority without direct administration. It underpinned the structure of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a>, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/majapahit-empire">Majapahit Empire</a> ruled much of the Indonesian archipelago through vassal relationships.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vassal.jpg" alt="Vassal" width="320" height="219" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Myrabella · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bayeux_Tapestry_scene23_Harold_sacramentum_fecit_Willelmo_duci.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
